        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): move Settings navigation to the sidebar and unify page width",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nSettings pages mix route-level horizontal settings navigation with page-local width and overflow behavior. This makes General, Channels, Debug, Logs, Appearance, Worktrees, and related Settings pages feel inconsistent, and some pages can keep wider or nested-scroll layouts than the rest of Settings.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nIn this PR, Settings route navigation moves into a Settings-only sidebar with grouped existing Settings routes, sidebar search, and a Back to OpenClaw exit. Settings pages also share a 980px content workspace, while only the outer clipped config wrapper that created nested scrolling is removed.\n\nLanguage/control reorganization is intentionally deferred, and internal card styling is preserved.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers get a consistent Settings workspace across existing Settings routes, can search and jump between Settings pages and indexed Settings blocks from the sidebar, and can leave Settings back to their previous non-Settings route. This is a layout/navigation change only.\n\n## Evidence\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node --import tsx scripts/control-ui-i18n.ts check`\n- `/Users/vyctor/Documents/openclaw/review-worktrees/pr-100932-control-ui-mock-fixtures/node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check ui/src/app/app-host.ts ui/src/components/app-sidebar.ts ui/src/styles/layout.css ui/src/e2e/sidebar-customization.e2e.test.ts ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts`\n- `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run ui/src/e2e/sidebar-customization.e2e.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts`\n\nUpdated in this refresh:\n\n- Rebased against current `main`.\n- Preserved Worktrees in the grouped Settings sidebar.\n- Settings routes ignore the persisted collapsed-sidebar shell class while keeping the preference for normal sidebar routes.\n- Added focused E2E coverage for persisted collapsed sidebar state on Settings.\n- Added focused E2E coverage for Settings search finding the proposed `Context Profile` block.\n- Updated Back to OpenClaw so Settings returns to the previous non-Settings route, with chat as fallback.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nDesktop Settings layout in this PR:\n\n![Desktop Settings sidebar layout](https://flowing-vow-rw6x.here.now/pr-100936-settings-sidebar-desktop.png)\n\nMobile Settings drawer in this PR:\n\n![Mobile Settings sidebar drawer](https://flowing-vow-rw6x.here.now/pr-100936-settings-sidebar-mobile.png)\n",
